          "annotations": [],
          "text": "The cart should descend, strike the domino, and topple it onto the flap\u2019s strike pad. That should overcome the hinge friction; the offset weight then drives the flap to its downward stop, letting the ball fall through the ring into the box.\n\nI would not accept the original as reliably satisfying the final resting condition. Its contacts use MuJoCo\u2019s default `condim=\"3\"`, so the specified rolling friction is inactive. The ball could retain rolling motion; wall impacts might stop it, but I have no measured run establishing that. The correction below enables rolling resistance. This is a file-based assessment, not a simulated result.\n\n```xml\n<mujoco model=\"cart_domino_flap_ball\">\n  <compiler angle=\"radian\" autolimits=\"true\"/>\n  <option timestep=\"0.002\" gravity=\"0 0 -9.81\" integrator=\"implicitfast\" iterations=\"100\" tolerance=\"1e-10\"/>\n  <size njmax=\"2000\" nconmax=\"400\"/>\n\n  <visual>\n    <headlight ambient=\"0.45 0.45 0.45\" diffuse=\"0.7 0.7 0.7\"/>\n    <global azimuth=\"135\" elevation=\"-25\"/>\n  </visual>\n\n  <worldbody>\n    <light name=\"overhead\" pos=\"0 -1 4\" dir=\"0 0 -1\" diffuse=\"0.8 0.8 0.8\"/>\n    <camera name=\"overview\" pos=\"2.7 -4 2.8\" xyaxes=\"0.83 0.56 0 -0.25 0.37 0.895\"/>\n\n    <geom name=\"floor\" type=\"plane\" size=\"5 5 0.1\" rgba=\"0.23 0.26 0.29 1\" friction=\"1 0.02 0.005\" solref=\"0.008 1\"/>\n\n    <!-- The slide joint guides the cart; these rail geoms visualize its path. -->\n    <body name=\"rail\" pos=\"-0.834026 -0.3 1.160718\" quat=\"0.965925826 0 0.258819045 0\">\n      <geom name=\"rail_bed\" type=\"box\" size=\"0.76 0.115 0.015\" contype=\"0\" conaffinity=\"0\" rgba=\"0.35 0.39 0.43 1\"/>\n      <geom name=\"rail_left_guide\" type=\"box\" pos=\"0 -0.13 0.045\" size=\"0.76 0.015 0.045\" contype=\"0\" conaffinity=\"0\" rgba=\"0.65 0.68 0.72 1\"/>\n      <geom name=\"rail_right_guide\" type=\"box\" pos=\"0 0.13 0.045\" size=\"0.76 0.015 0.045\" contype=\"0\" conaf